# PinkDog Website Development Guidelines

## Instagram Integration Implementation

### Current Status
- Instagram feed hook (`useInstagramFeed.ts`) has been implemented to fetch posts from Instagram API
- `InstagramGallery` component has been built to display Instagram images
- Fallback images have been added for cases when the Instagram API fails or when no token is provided
- Social media links have been added to the Footer and About Us sections

### Pending Tasks
- Instagram Access Token needs to be configured in the environment variables:
  - Create or update `.env.local` file with valid Instagram Graph API token
  - Format: `NEXT_PUBLIC_IG_TOKEN=your_instagram_access_token_here`
- Real Instagram images will appear once the token is properly configured
- Testing across different screen sizes to ensure responsive behavior

### Technical Requirements
- The Instagram feed uses the Instagram Graph API
- Access token must have permissions for `instagram_basic` and `pages_show_list`
- Fallback to static images if API fails to ensure UI consistency

### Implementation Notes
- Ensure your Instagram account is a Business or Creator account
- Link your Instagram account to a Facebook page
- Generate a long-lived token to minimize token refresh requirements
- For testing, you can use the fallback images already configured
